{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow","id":792806,"title":"Consume Not Thy Children - Lairing in the Shadow","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-25T12:57:49-08:00","id":792806,"title":"Consume Not Thy Children - Lairing in the Shadow","content":"A line of inquiry that's been on my mind for the last couple of weeks has been how some of the Begotten might regularly interact with spirits in the Hisil, because it seems like there's an awful lot of room for such a game to roam as far as becoming one of the movers and shakers of the setting.<br /> <br /> Setting aside matters of basic Kinship tricks, a Beast in the Shadow counts as a source of Essence Resonant for spirits whose nature aligns with their Hunger and Family (and can therefore logically steer other spirits toward that resonance by allowing them to feed on that Essence), can engage in Family Dinner with spirits engaging in predation, and can claim areas of the Shadow as Chambers by getting an exceptional success on a Nightmare roll or witnessing a loss of Integrity in that locale.<br /> <br /> It's a fair bit of a side-path from conventional play, seeing as Skeleton Key and Family Resemblance don't allow the Begotten to detect spirits in Twilight or recognize loci, but a game set in a place with werewolves or a few prominent Claimed or Hosts might provide a decent starting point and from there the conflict between growing your Legend and maintaining your Life while running and/or supporting a brood of spirits could prove fun.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any thoughts or ideas or questions on this notion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T13:55:26-08:00","id":792822,"title":"","content":"It sounds like a very interesting game to play. The only problem that I could see would be the one you mentioned, the Beast's inability to sense Loci. <br /> If a Beast created a Chamber from the Shadow, do you think it would be feasible to have some kind of link between that chamber and the Shadow. Perhaps similar to a Verge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T13:58:12-08:00","id":792824,"title":"","content":"It would be interesting if the brood didn't have Werewolf allies, but had to deal with them as borderline enemies, with the Beasts just wanting to mosey along with their newfound spirit friends and the werewolves regarding them as loose cannons, beings unbound by the Oath of the Moon. I wonder if such a brood might get involved with the Pure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T14:48:44-08:00","id":792837,"title":"","content":"As an idea for how a Beast could get involved with the Shadow:<br /> A Ravager burns down a building to feed. One of the fire-spirits drawn to the blaze takes a liking to this seeming mortal who can feed it so and tries to Ride it. It worms its way into where the human's soul should be. Instead, it finds a burning forest and a dragon with golden scales and steel talons. The spirit escapes, but is fascinated by the creature, following him around, feeding when he feeds.<br /> Until one day, the human turns around, looks at the spirit and says &quot;I know you're there. I saw you in the smoke and the fire. What do you want from me?&quot; And the spirit shows him a way into its home, into the Shadow and shows itself to the Man-who-is-a-Dragon. And the Dragon-who-is-a-Man opens a Path and shows the spirit his dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T15:53:13-08:00","id":792856,"title":"","content":"I don't think Beasts get any facility with First Tongue, regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T20:46:03-08:00","id":792925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow?p=792856#post792856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Beasts get any facility with First Tongue, regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps you could reflect it with a Merit. Maybe a refined version of the Spirit Tongue Merit from Book of Spirits?<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if the Beast happens to have the Wolf-Blooded Tell that allows for communicating with spirits (not to mention Piercing Eyes), then it's a moot point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 12-25-2015, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T23:03:41-08:00","id":792954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow?p=792925#post792925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps you could reflect it with a Merit. Maybe a refined version of the Spirit Tongue Merit from Book of Spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>First Tongue is an eligible subject for the Language Merit in 2e and spirits often pick up the local human speech regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T00:03:06-08:00","id":792985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow?p=792954#post792954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First Tongue is an eligible subject for the Language Merit in 2e and spirits often pick up the local human speech regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>That kinda goes over the whole Tell about it. If it was as easy taking language merit, when the human speaking apparatus isn't even aptly constructed for it's use, if it ever was.<br /> <br /> But Beasts do get supernatural merits, so Advanced language it'd be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T00:27:56-08:00","id":793002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow?p=792985#post792985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That kinda goes over the whole Tell about it. If it was as easy taking language merit, when the human speaking apparatus isn't even aptly constructed for it's use, if it ever was.<br /> <br /> But Beasts do get supernatural merits, so Advanced language it'd be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd entertain an argument that the First Tongue would be easier for a Beast merged with its Horror, whether through Lair Resonance or Inheritance, what with their stronger link to the Astral, and their more ideal forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T00:40:32-08:00","id":793007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow?p=792824#post792824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be interesting if the brood didn't have Werewolf allies, but had to deal with them as borderline enemies, with the Beasts just wanting to mosey along with their newfound spirit friends and the werewolves regarding them as loose cannons, beings unbound by the Oath of the Moon. I wonder if such a brood might get involved with the Pure.</div> </div> </div> </div>The broader problem comes from running into a hostile &quot;bigger fish&quot; while Gorged, particularly at higher Lair \u2014 unless you can engineer a workaround or grow your power base sufficiently to claim dominance, your options amount to capping your Satiety at the levels where Heroes are a more prominent hazard, using Kinship to try to succeed whichever minor god you've had the poor fortune to encounter, or taking refuge in your Life while you try to regroup.<br /> <br /> If you meet the Rabid Wolf on the road, hide, basically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow?p=792985#post792985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That kinda goes over the whole Tell about it. If it was as easy taking language merit, when the human speaking apparatus isn't even aptly constructed for it's use, if it ever was.<br /> <br /> But Beasts do get supernatural merits, so Advanced language it'd be.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tell comes packaged with a Beat generator and is a Tell. Does Iron Skin &quot;go over&quot; Liar's Skin because both provide Armor? That werewolves have a set of other forms better suited to speaking the First Tongue doesn't change the fact that the human speaking apparatus can manage a rough attempt at the language in 1e and this is borne out by how 2e has presented it thusfar \u2014 &quot;the Language (First Tongue) Merit&quot; is part of the starting werewolf PC template and the Unchained can speak it as easily as any other language. I also find it undesirable for one's ability to speak the First Tongue to be something that can temporarily <i>fall off</i> at Satiety 10, particularly given that there's also no mundane prerequisite Merit to build off of.<br /> <br /> <br /> Taking a line of inquiry drawn from the matter of resonance, what sort of spirits might Beasts of each Hunger attract? The Families offer fairly straightforward aesthetics to adapt towards, but what kind of symbolism beyond the obvious does a Nemesis or a Collector pull in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T00:46:28-08:00","id":793009,"title":"","content":"You're quoting all supernatural implications for having aptitude in First Tongue, tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T00:55:24-08:00","id":793012,"title":"","content":"You might have to make some kind of 'house rule' regarding the speaking to and seeing the spirit. Maybe you could have a thing that makes it so that if you have Kinship with a given spirit (or other incorporeal being) you can communicate with it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T00:58:07-08:00","id":793014,"title":"","content":"If that idea works for you, I could have a go at writing it up. Any ideas for a name?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T06:44:29-08:00","id":793063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking a line of inquiry drawn from the matter of resonance, what sort of spirits might Beasts of each Hunger attract? The Families offer fairly straightforward aesthetics to adapt towards, but what kind of symbolism beyond the obvious does a Nemesis or a Collector pull in?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I imagine a Collector might associate with or rise in the ranks of the spirits of whatever they collect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T07:13:13-08:00","id":793071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow?p=793007#post793007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Taking a line of inquiry drawn from the matter of resonance, what sort of spirits might Beasts of each Hunger attract? The Families offer fairly straightforward aesthetics to adapt towards, but what kind of symbolism beyond the obvious does a Nemesis or a Collector pull in?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would imagine that a Nemesis would make enemies of the spirits of the transgressions that he is punishing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T07:35:37-08:00","id":793078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow?p=793007#post793007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking a line of inquiry drawn from the matter of resonance, what sort of spirits might Beasts of each Hunger attract? The Families offer fairly straightforward aesthetics to adapt towards, but what kind of symbolism beyond the obvious does a Nemesis or a Collector pull in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tyrants would definitely have spirits of obedience, servitude, and the like flocking behind them. Conversely, expect spirits reflecting concepts like tyranny, domination, and conquest trying to oppose him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T09:17:12-08:00","id":793127,"title":"","content":"I wonder if a powerful enough Beast might be able to set up something a bit like a spirit Court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T17:31:40-08:00","id":793333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow?p=793009#post793009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're quoting all supernatural implications for having aptitude in First Tongue, tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm quoting the reasons why the pseudo-spiritual groups with an innate connection to the Shadow and a natural facility for language have particular fluency in the Tongue, neither of which contradicts the facts that werewolves in Hishu and demons in Cover aren't physiologically different from humans in a fashion that affects their ability to manage a functional pronunciation of the language and that First Tongue is made by retro-applying a trend in human linguistics to a human language. That spirits speak the language does not make it a Supernatural Merit, much less an Advanced Merit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow?p=793063#post793063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, I imagine a Collector might associate with or rise in the ranks of the spirits of whatever they collect.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would certainly mesh with the trend of spirits asking for favors that promote their respective phenomena or diminish their rivals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow?p=793071#post793071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would imagine that a Nemesis would make enemies of the spirits of the transgressions that he is punishing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see it going either way, really, given the way Hunger for Punishment works; how a friendly connection manifests mostly boils down to who's calling the shots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow?p=793078#post793078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tyrants would definitely have spirits of obedience, servitude, and the like flocking behind them. Conversely, expect spirits reflecting concepts like tyranny, domination, and conquest trying to oppose him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like these being complementary concepts suggests a higher likelihood of internal division within the brood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow?p=793127#post793127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if a powerful enough Beast might be able to set up something a bit like a spirit Court.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the idea!<br /> <br /> Ravagers are fairly easy to figure out as well \u2014 spirits born from disasters come to mind immediately \u2014 but what are the likely nuances of the spiritual partners to those who Hunger for Prey?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T17:57:29-08:00","id":793346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow#post792806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a fair bit of a side-path from conventional play, seeing as Skeleton Key and Family Resemblance don't allow the Begotten to detect spirits in Twilight or recognize loci, but a game set in a place with werewolves or a few prominent Claimed or Hosts might provide a decent starting point and from there the conflict between growing your Legend and maintaining your Life while running and/or supporting a brood of spirits could prove fun.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any thoughts or ideas or questions on this notion?</div> </div> </div> </div> You don't need a Skeleton Key. You can simply open a Primordial Pathway directly to the Hisil. The Skeleton Key and Family Resemblence are two of what I call &quot;crossover enablers.&quot; Abilities designed so that, when interacting with other splats, you don't get left behind when they go realm hopping. In the case of a spirit, you can just use Primordial Pathways to get around easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T18:21:00-08:00","id":793356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow?p=793333#post793333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm quoting the reasons why the pseudo-spiritual groups with an innate connection to the Shadow and a natural facility for language have particular fluency in the Tongue, neither of which contradicts the facts that werewolves in Hishu and demons in Cover aren't physiologically different from humans in a fashion that affects their ability to manage a functional pronunciation of the language and that First Tongue is made by retro-applying a trend in human linguistics to a human language. That spirits speak the language does not make it a Supernatural Merit, much less an Advanced Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">To quote Tongues:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sometimes strange, profane, and alien words fall out of the Wolf-Blooded\u2019s mouth instead of the language she\u2019s trying to speak. Anytime a character fails a roll that involves speaking or singing, he can turn it into a dramatic failure. He takes a Beat and suffers the results of stumbling mutters accidentally said in the language of the Shadow. <b>To humans, </b><b>it sounds horrific and impossible. To werewolves and spirits, it </b><b>seems impossible that a human mouth could form the words </b><b>that the Wolf-Blooded just has.</b> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> Then you have that no published character ever has had Language (First Tongue) in the form of a merit. Then you have that Unchained do not, in fact have dominion over first tongue, for the same reason they lack any fluency in dead tongues. Your argument is invalid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T20:45:51-08:00","id":793398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow?p=793346#post793346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You don't need a Skeleton Key. You can simply open a Primordial Pathway directly to the Hisil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside the sporadic evidence that Primordial Pathways can't trivially get you wherever you need to go and function best as return shortcuts, the ability doesn't come with a cosmological directory. You rather need to know the place exists, is my point in bringing up those particular blind spots in the Kinship toolkit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow?p=793356#post793356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you have that no published character ever has had Language (First Tongue) in the form of a merit. Then you have that Unchained do not, in fact have dominion over first tongue, for the same reason they lack any fluency in dead tongues. Your argument is invalid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey Eph?<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon: the Descent Core Rulebook, p183, &quot;Natural Aptitude&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons only speak native languages, however. No one in modern times grows up speaking ancient Sumerian or Latin, despite the fact that some scholars might have enough skill with these languages to understand them. Likewise, while enthusiasts might develop enough facility with artificial languages such as Tolkein\u2019s Elvish, no one speaks the language as a native. Demons can learn to speak such languages through study, but not through Natural Aptitude. <b>By the same token, demons can use Natural Aptitude to speak First Tongue (the \u201cnative language\u201d of spirits)</b>, but not High Speech (the mystical tongue of the mages, no longer in common or conversational use).</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf: the Forsaken Second Edition Core Rulebook, p57, &quot;First Tongue&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves share a proto-language with spirits called Uremehir, or the First Tongue. <b>Legend holds that humans, spirits, and werewolves all used the language prior to the breaking of Pangaea.</b> Immediately after the First Change, a werewolf can understand Uremehir, at least enough to get the gist of the speaker\u2019s message. <b>He can learn fluency in the language from another Uratha who already knows Uremehir, or by bargaining for the favor from a spirit. Although spirits and werewolves speak slightly different dialects of First Tongue (due to the restrictions of the werewolves\u2019 vocal cords), they can understand each other readily enough.</b><br /> For the Uratha, communication differs by form. <b>Hishu form can obviously speak any human language the werewolf knows, and can communicate roughly in First Tongue.</b> Uratha speak Uremehir most fluently while wearing the Dalu or Gauru forms.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF 2e Core, p87, &quot;Step Six: Add Merits&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, every character receives one dot of Totem, <b>and the Language (First Tongue) Merit.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF 2e Core, p272, &quot;Voyager Membership&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Initiate (\u2022): Initiates receive an Occult Specialty in Spirit Tongues. <b>This allows them to understand and use rudimentary First Tongue. They can only communicate very simple ideas with their human mouths.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF 2e Core, p291, &quot;Character Creation&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For your teenage characters in this story, <b>anything particularly strange, like seeing spirits or speaking the First Tongue</b>, should have just started happening. A Tell coming up in-scene should add to the Tension pool.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> If you're not going to contribute to the actual topic, step off.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyone have any ideas for spirits kin to Predators?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T21:38:23-08:00","id":793414,"title":"","content":"As for a spirit that would feel at home in the resonance of a predator beast, there are spirits of predation, although they were only mentioned in the werewolf chroniclers guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T04:14:35-08:00","id":793501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow?p=793398#post793398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting aside the sporadic evidence that Primordial Pathways can't trivially get you wherever you need to go and function best as return shortcuts, the ability doesn't come with a cosmological directory. You rather need to know the place exists, is my point in bringing up those particular blind spots in the Kinship toolkit.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I don't quite see it the same way, so I'm going to have to disagree. You do need to know about the existance of other places first, admittedly. However, that's what Beast society is for. I see no reason that starting characters are knowledgable about the other realms. <br /> <br /> Primordial Pathways can open up to other realms, but they have to resonate with your Lair. I'm going to assume that, if youre' hunting with the spirits, you have something that resonates with them. P.P.s aren't teleportation, so they rarely will get you to an exact coordinate you want to get to, but I rather think that you don't need to if we're just talking about crossing the Gauntlet. Its not easy (-2 penalty) but its doable. There wouldn't be a penalty if it wasn't viable.<br /> <br /> I'm really not seeing blind spots here. The knowledge is available (unless arbitrarily forbidden by ST), and the ability is there. You can start with kinship to spirits as per the starting Satiety rules.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyone have any ideas for spirits kin to Predators? </div> </div> </div> All of them? The Hisil is a realm of predation, so every spirit is a kind of predator. Its the reminants of the Hunter's Paradise, after all. The Underworld is a world of entropy and nihilsm, resonating with Ruin. The Hedge/Faerie would resonate with Collectors, I'd argue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T13:03:43-08:00","id":793749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/792806-consume-not-thy-children-lairing-in-the-shadow?p=793501#post793501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primordial Pathways can open up to other realms, but they have to resonate with your Lair. I'm going to assume that, if youre' hunting with the spirits, you have something that resonates with them. P.P.s aren't teleportation, so they rarely will get you to an exact coordinate you want to get to, but I rather think that you don't need to if we're just talking about crossing the Gauntlet. Its not easy (-2 penalty) but its doable. There wouldn't be a penalty if it wasn't viable.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem stems from the <i>other</i> penalty \u2014 it's not clear whether, for instance, the Shadow's iteration of one of your materially-derived Chambers counts as having Exact similarity to its Earthly counterpart, particularly in urban locations where the thicker Gauntlet translates to a greater degree of abstraction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm really not seeing blind spots here. The knowledge is available (unless arbitrarily forbidden by ST), and the ability is there. </div> </div> </div>Assuming a Doylist view in response to a Watsonian look at the information granted by the abilities alone. Without encountering a Materialized spirit or a locus bridging the Gauntlet a Beast with no convenient contact is just as unaware of the spirit world as any mortal.<br /> <br /> The Begotten do not possess the ability to instantiate the requisite twists of fate that bring a realm to their awareness and I'd hope it was clear when talking about the problems of running into a stronger spirit and maintaining a power base that the assumptions of the game are not such that the local Shadow is a well-known asset to the Begotten in whatever setting these hypotheticals take place in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All of them? </div> </div> </div>That's exactly why I mentioned nuance. I was looking for specific examples that might be particularly well-suited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-27-2015, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}